title: Conductor external dependency — claude -p / Agent SDK pricing in flux (watch-item)
summary: 'Anthropic emailed (2026-06-15) that the previously-announced change moving Claude Agent SDK / `claude -p` / third-party-apps-built-on-the-SDK OFF subscription rate limits and onto a dedicated monthly credit is NOT happening today — they''re reworking the plan "to better support how users build with Claude subscriptions." This is DIRECTLY tied to the Conductor revival: `claude -p` is Conductor''s engine, so its metering model is the product''s economic substrate. Favorable-for-now (the rework targets exactly our use case: building on subscriptions), but a live dependency to monitor in case we must pivot the cost/messaging model.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#claude-stream-session'
  - '#conductor'
learnings:
  - 'Today, Conductor''s fleet of `claude -p` sessions draws from the user''s SUBSCRIPTION rate limits, not a separate credit — confirmed by the `rate_limit_event` in our own stream-json output (rateLimitType: five_hour). N concurrent ATRIUM sessions share that rolling window.'
  - The deferred change would have split claude -p / Agent SDK usage to a dedicated monthly credit. Anthropic delayed it and is reworking to better support subscription-based building — favorable for Conductor (we ARE that use case).
  - 'Design implication: stay billing-model-agnostic. Don''t hard-architect around either model. Keep per-session cost visible (ATRIUM footer already shows $cost/turn). Assume usage may move between ''subscription rate limit'' and ''metered credit''.'
  - 'Pivot triggers to watch: (a) claude -p usage moved to a separate paid credit (changes cost story + ''runs on your subscription'' messaging); (b) rate-limit tightening that makes multi-session fleets impractical on a subscription; (c) Agent SDK becoming the required/cheaper path vs spawning the CLI.'
